Who You Are and What You’ll Do &nbsp;

You are a detail-oriented accounting professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills who can navigate complex, non-standard contracts and billing scenarios. You ensure contract terms and system records are accurate and complete, partnering with cross-functional teams to support proper invoicing and revenue recognition in compliance with ASC 606. You exercise sound judgment and adapt to unique client requirements across the bookings-to-cash cycle. Your responsibilities will include: &nbsp;

• Review Closed Won opportunities, contracts, SOWs, and Salesforce records for accuracy and completeness. &nbsp;

• Validate contract terms, billing schedules, and non-standard transactions in collaboration with Sales, Deal Desk, Delivery, and Infrastructure. &nbsp;

• Ensure accurate project setup, invoicing, and revenue recognition in compliance with ASC 606. &nbsp;

• Manage billing milestones, client invoicing, purchase orders, payment reconciliation, and collections. &nbsp;

• Maintain client financial records, payment terms, billing contacts, and sales tax information in Salesforce. &nbsp;

• Audit projects during Pending Finance Review to ensure accurate invoicing and revenue recognition. &nbsp;

• Process employee expense reports and coordinate monthly reimbursements and receivables with Payroll. &nbsp;

• Manage sales tax rates, audit tax allocation accuracy, and coordinate potential tax obligations with external advisors. &nbsp;

• Resolve billing discrepancies and non-standard contract scenarios, exercising independent judgment to ensure accuracy throughout the bookings-to-cash cycle. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your Education and Experience &nbsp;

The following is a list of skills and traits that describe you. If you have most of these, we’d like to speak to you: &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field, or equivalent relevant experience. &nbsp;

• Strong interest in finance and accounting, with an aptitude for working with numbers. &nbsp;

• Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Excel. &nbsp;

• Experience reviewing contracts, Statements of Work (SOWs), amendments, purchase orders, and billing terms is preferred but not required. &nbsp;

• Experience with financial systems and business tools such as Salesforce, Professional Services Automation (PSA) platforms, Certinia, or similar systems. &nbsp;

